From a491c40267dea36c0ad2dcd3376d6f4548804906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:05:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] demo: add SARJ as a third detector next to Baseline and P3

SARJ (leenalotaibi-source/sarj @ c4611c9): echo-aware acoustics,
caller-relative level, leaky speech evidence and an Arabic words layer
(offline Whisper tiny: free transcript + keyword spotting of stop and
listener words). Official real-time dev run of the exact files served
here: Core 96.83 (R 0.961, S 0.969), 1 false stop, 0 misses, 0 protocol
errors (experiments/evidence/v3-c4611c9-rt).

- server: multi-file detectors are pinned file by file ("files" in the
  model spec); any changed module disables the detector instead of
  running it. A detector may report which layers really loaded
  (demo_note), shown in its description. Internal id "v3"; the page
  shows "SARJ" and the commit.
- page: detectors are data-driven (cards, headline, results table,
  timeline lanes, benchmark table); SARJ is optional and shown only when
  the server has it, Baseline and P3 remain required.
- Dockerfile/requirements: faster-whisper, Whisper tiny fetched at build
  time; without it SARJ runs on acoustics alone and says so.
- tests: three pinned detectors, SARJ refuses a changed module, three
  benchmark rows equal to runs.json (146 passed).
- measured in public mode: 406 MB peak with 4 simultaneous playbacks
  (SARJ_DEMO_MAX_SESSIONS stays 12).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BHwakaZ8PDY7RCXJVGEr6w
